cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Pyskyfire: a simulation framework for liquid propellant rocket engines"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ask Haugerud"
    family-names: Hovik
    email: ask@askhaugerudhovik.no
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3781-4639"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ask-hovik/pyskyfire"
url: "https://ask-hovik.github.io/pyskyfire/"
abstract: >-
  Pyskyfire is a Python based, object-oriented, openly licensed simulation
  framework for regeneratively cooled liquid propellant rocket engines. It
  covers engine contour generation from first-principles inputs, multi-pass
  cooling channel geometry, chemical equilibrium combustion modelling,
  regenerative cooling analysis of thrust chambers, pump, turbine and ducting
  models, and steady state solution of the complete engine cycle.
keywords:
  - rocket engine
  - liquid propellant
  - regenerative cooling
  - propulsion
  - engine cycle analysis
  - simulation
